RasMol 2.6-beta-2 is Copyright (c) Roger Sayle, 1992-1999.

RasMol was originally developed at the University of Edinburgh's
Biocomputing Research Unit, and subsequently at the Biomolecular
Structures Group, Glaxo Wellcome Research & Development, Stevenage,
Hertfordshire, UK.

From the original RasMol distribution (UMass RasMol source page,
https://www.umass.edu/microbio/rasmol/srccode.htm, mirroring Roger
Sayle's University of Edinburgh FTP site, the canonical source):

    "The source code is public domain and freely distributable
     provided that the original author is suitably acknowledged."

This repository is a modernized fork of RasMol 2.6-beta-2
(RasMol26b2.tar.gz; the pristine tarball is kept at
source/RasMol26b2.tar.gz for reference). See README.RASMOL-ORIGINAL
for the original README and ChangeLog for the full dated history of
changes, both the original 1992-1999 development and everything
added by this fork.

All modifications in this repository -- including but not limited to
the SDL2 display backend, the mmCIF/PDBx reader, file-format
auto-detection, and the various bug fixes described in ChangeLog --
are distributed under these same terms: freely usable, modifiable
and distributable, provided Roger Sayle is acknowledged as RasMol's
original author.

No warranty of any kind is given or implied.
